{title: Every Morning}
{artist: Daniel Sullivan}
{key: E}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 74}

Verse 1
Every morning, it’s just the same
I bow my head in Jesus name
And when I’m done thanking you
I always ask for a favor or two
And then I go about my day

Verse 2
And then I go wandering away
Now by the time I go to bed
I’ve gone back on what I said
All those things, about lovin’ you
Could you tell by what I say and do
Oh wicked man that I am
Who will save me from sin

Chorus
Jesus, you deliver me from all my shame
I love you Lord, and I surrender to you
I confess, and you are faithful to forgive my sins
Now I rejoice, that your mercies are new
Every morning

Verse 3
Now my conscience, is clean and new
My desire is set on you
And I will walk in the light you give
And I will die, so that you may live

Chorus
Jesus, you deliver me from all my shame
I love you Lord, and I surrender to you
I confess, and you are faithful to forgive my sins
Now I rejoice, that your mercies are new
Every morning

Verse 4
Every morning, it's just the same
I'm alive in Jesus name
